msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:9
#: 9ba40cf48cb84fbf9f45b198de95dfa1
msgid "**ARCHIVED ARTICLE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:11
#: b4729540ce534d0a85e7797fe571f72c
msgid "This article is for creating a quadcopter using the PX4FMU only, which is one approach for creating a very small autopilot. `Arsovtech <http://arsovtech.com/?p=1447>`__ have created a small Pixhawk based board that is much more popular with the community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:17
#: 36ddccf2b86e4fea9939e99fc2c4e857
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:19
#: aa87444f11504f298bcf8b9adfb47f59
msgid "**Bill Of Materials:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:21
#: d0727306da88431bb8a3da4346e01bf3
msgid "Copter firmware version 3.1 and later supports only the combined system of the PX4 FMU and PX4 IO board; the FMU-only system is no longer supported. Purchase a PX4 FMU kit from 3DRobotics LINK_BROKEN and a PX4 I/O board LINK_BROKEN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:25
#: 8159b7bd6b2b440b9c283042bd7a0d9a
msgid "A special cable that fits into the PX4's main \"Multi\" connector will allow you to perform the primary wiring and it is available from 3DRobotics LINK_BROKEN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:28
#: 5abbeeba98d64685a441dba60402aab2
msgid "If you choose, you can cut off the single pin connectors and solder directly to the necessary locations and trim back the excess wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:30
#: a30d46119b934dedbf35f0e46ea3c258
msgid "Use the 4 supplied nylon standoffs to mount the PX4FMU to a piece of scrap plastic or fiberglass sheet the same size as the FMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:33
#: c2d158557bf44b768984acc781193d0c
msgid "Mount the board to your copter with four 3/4\" squares of Kyosho Zeal gel or double sided foam tape to provide vibration isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:36
#: 96a246f694784c65b23b204ed9b61367
msgid "**Mount your PX4-FMU board in a central location on top of your QuadCopter.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:39
#: e44d1a1aa8674b0e84bc911d73377b8d
msgid "The PX4FMU board Normally has the SD card on top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:40
#: 2f0ddca12fa64f709067b044f0477ea3
msgid "It can sometimes be advantageous to mount the PX4FMU with the other side up for better LED observation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:42
#: 3cfa19b9fbec47438ee3472bfc992f21
msgid "If you do mount the PX4FMU board with the Component side up it will be necessary to set the \"Board Orientation (AHRS_ORIENTATION)\" parameter to \"Roll 180\" in the Advanced Parameter List in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:46
#: 92a7564ca60248029447fd3e288427b2
msgid "The arrow labeled \"FRONT\" should be facing to the front of the aircraft (also the large black board interconnect connector)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:48
#: 9a558ec8df394668969edc78c3c4279c
msgid "If you use the vibration dampers suggested above it is best to put a small O-ring on top of the damper and under the PX4 Board before fastening it \"gently\" down with the supplied nuts to prevent damage to the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:52
#: 0b38d48684c745b9918ed3f24b81ea28
msgid "In fact, these dampers may not provide adequate damping and you should review the Wiki section on vibration control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:55
#: ce7cde76c3144be4af2780a2318d5053
msgid "**Mount the GPS facing up with an unobstructed \"view\" of the sky**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:57
#: f3613de015224ae2959d32ebd83fb9dd
msgid "The GPS can be mounted on a short riser to give it the widest satellite access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:61
#: cdb7d8f9498e4b5595cad69437821dca
msgid "PX4-FMU Only Wiring Diagram for QuadCopters using a PPM-SUM receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:67
#: dafa1505db2e4eb781684acbd4e277a1
msgid "Wiring the PX4FMU Board to Your QuadCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:69
#: 1a0265c3518a45f4b5808bd79c8cdf19
msgid "**Use heavy gauge wire to interconnect the ESC's Ground and power leads to a Battery Connector.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:72
#: f7c1c6119fac424299c5ec70f1036fd3
msgid "A Power Distribution board can also be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:74
#: 249d82abfac04dd3ae85b8ced1c78876
msgid "**Connect your BEC (5 volt power supply) power in leads to the battery input leads.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:78
#: 9caa3acc9aed43419b64820a30ee8cfb
msgid "Connect the BEC Ground output to the PX4's Ground (Multi connector pin 15)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:80
#: 5623e71208b547ae9fba10ef60cbee06
msgid "Connect the BEC Power output to the PX4's power In (Multi connector pin 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:82
#: 67abbfcdc60b435d984b33c8a279ac15
msgid "**NOTE!** Instead of a separate BEC as shown, the power and ground leads (signal side) from one of your ESCs that contains a BEC can be wired to the Multi connectors pins 1 and 15 to provide PX4 board power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:87
#: 45eb59d8180d4435a4d061701be87c0e
msgid "**The PPM-SUM receiver may be wired with a connecting cable as shown in the diagram above.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:90
#: 5fbd9e479dec4cef80d3205d1a63acf2
msgid "Or the PPM-SUM signal and power and ground leads from the 15 pin DF13 \"Multi\" connector may be directly wired to a 3 pin servo/receiver connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:93
#: d1dfeb325951412081b4195ce21530f0
msgid "Connect your PPM-Sum RC receivers signal wire to pin 6 of the Multi connector on the PX4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:95
#: 334fb4dd5d194bdeb98ece27178b1e48
msgid "Connect the PPM-SUM RC Receivers Ground lead to pin 15 of the Multi connector on the PX4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:97
#: e1b58efb6146479580cc3756af006dd4
msgid "Connect the PPM-SUM RC Receivers Power lead to pin 1 of the Multi connector on the PX4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:100
#: 32cabffd3d724e06b681625a4e64a665
msgid "**Wire the PX4FMU board's 4 servo out signals to the ESC control inputs.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:103
#: bdf8684039d34baeb8eb625d3afc4a65
msgid "The wires can be put together with connectors as shown in the diagram or solder and heat shrink tubing can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:105
#: 6d734c65d128472eae4b2f075f7ed9f9
msgid "Wire PX4FMU PWM control 4 (Multi Connector pin 9) to The ESC signal in for Motor 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:107
#: 53789bf83600472fb9ad6749971479a0
msgid "Wire PX4FMU PWM control 2 (Multi Connector pin 10) to The ESC signal in for Motor 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:109
#: d7b3c753be1d46d48661ae15a9aec265
msgid "Wire PX4FMU PWM control 1 (Multi Connector pin 11) to The ESC signal in for Motor 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:111
#: 5c414f5b77b64edc8b71f6ce5dcee1e4
msgid "Wire PX4FMU PWM control 3 (Multi Connector pin 12) to The ESC signal in for Motor 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:114
#: 5a3ad465406841b3a946723f355dab37
msgid "**Run a wire from the PX4FMU's Battery Monitor connection (Multi Connector pin 5) to the positive battery power lead.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:116
#: ccb4fa0c292647faa470a977cc6a21e6
msgid "**Note! The cable that is supplied in the plastic envelope with the UBLOX GPS which has white 6 pin connectors on both ends is NOT the correct cable for the PX4**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:120
#: 1281dde688b440edb28f99ce7520221b
msgid "The correct longer cable is provided in a separate envelope and has a 5 pin \"beige\" connector on one end and a 6 pin white connector on the other end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:123
#: 62501080859948c9b27a4488a87f4a69
msgid "Plug the correct GPS cable's white 6 pin connector into the 6 pin socket on the GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:125
#: cf8fe1a240c848b7a76e2c372a401ec6
msgid "Plug the beige 5 pin connector into the PX4's 5 pin GPS socket which is next to the 15 pin DF13 Mini connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:128
#: 108dfa5e62b347e592694e1eefd814e1
msgid "**Plug the 2 pin connector attached to the lead supplied with the buzzer into the buzzer socket on the side of the PX4FMU board that has the SD card holder on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:131
#: 671b2842efc64300b781d66f49c3f07d
msgid "In Mission Planner in the Complete Parameter List it will be necessary for you to set the **BRD_SAFETYENABLE** parameter to 0 = off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:135
#: 72cd374b22a44a23914d498aba2e5131
msgid "This is because the safety switch connects to the IO board's on board microcontroller and there is no switch for the PX4FMU only."
msgstr ""

